b. Speak about the impact of the behaviour, focusing on the behaviour − not the 
person. 
c. Listen to understand and acknowledge the viewpoint of the other person 
involved. 
d. Work together to find an agreement on how to resolve the issue through better 
communication, mutual understanding, and possibly developing a plan to avoid 
such impacts in the future. 
 
