on an ad hoc basis (i.e., the Appeals Panel should be formed to address appeals on an as-
needed basis rather than members being appointed for a set term). 
2. An Appeals Panel will normally consist of all members being present. Should any member 
not be able to attend, the Vice-President, Student Life and Leadership, or Designate, shall 
appoint an ad hoc member from the same constituency of the missing panel member. 
3. No member of the Appeals Panel will have served on the Student Code of Conduct 
Complaints Review Panel that heard the original case. 
4. Students have the right, before the merits of a complaint are heard, to challenge the 
