APPENDIX J – RECORDS AND RECORDS RETENTION 
Records of charges and sanctions, other than suspension or expulsion, will not be placed in a 
student’s academic record. Records of informal resolutions will be kept as part of student’s 
non-academic file until their graduation, after which such records will be destroyed. 
Records of formal resolutions, including charges and sanctions, will be maintained as 
confidential records in the Office of the Vice-President, Student Life and Leadership, for up to 
seven (7) years after the student(s)’ graduation, after which the records shall be destroyed. In 
cases where an individual ceases to be a student, all records of formal resolution including Sole 
Decision-Maker; Student Code of Conduct - Complaints Review Panel, or College Appeals Panel 
