investigation, and decision-making process; 
c. has the right to know reasons for a decision under this Code; and, 
d. has a right to appeal provided there are reasonable grounds for such appeal based 
on a reasonable apprehension of bias or that another breach of natural justice has 
taken place. 
Offence: Behaviour or actions by students that breach this Code or fall short of the College’s 
standard for student responsibilities. 
Penalties/Sanctions: Refers to measures taken to address breaches that fall below the 
expected standards of behaviour. They are applied primarily to correct behaviour rather than to 
punish behaviour. 
Reasonable Apprehension of Bias: A test to determine whether a decision has been unduly 
influenced by bias. 
