2. After meeting with the Respondent to outline the nature of the complaint and the 
Complainant’s desire to resolve the matter informally, the Vice-President, Student Life and 
Leadership, or Designate, or appointed facilitator(s), will meet with the Complainant, the 
Respondent, and any relevant witness(es), separately or jointly as required to facilitate the 
process. The process allows for multiple meetings, if required, provided the meetings 
remain constructive and are working positively to resolve the matter. The purpose of the 
meeting(s) is: 
i. 
to better understand the nature and impact of the harm; 
ii. 
to make the Respondent aware of the harmful impact on the Complainant; 
and 
iii. 
to assess the potential for arriving at a mutually agreeable outcome that 
