decided by the relevant 
College representative. 
Appeals of any such 
decision are to be made to 
the representative’s 
College Supervisor and 
any decision by the 
College Supervisor shall be 
deemed as final and not 
subject to further appeal. 
All incidents must be 
reported to the Vice-
President, Student Life 
and Leadership office and 
may form the basis of a 
complaint under the 
Student Code of Conduct. 
Level II − Behaviours which 
endanger the safety or security 
of Loyalist College community 
members or property, or that 
may be harmful to the physical 
or psychological well-being of 
community members. 
Examples may 
include, but are 
not limited to: 
- 
Bullying and 
harassing 
conduct 
- 
Damage to 
Loyalist College 
or community 
member’s 
property. 
- 
Threatening 
behaviour 
- 
Aggressive 
outbursts, 
either verbal or 
physical 
 
Depending on severity, the 
sanctions may be, but are not 
limited to: 
- 
Alcohol probation 
- 
