Level III – Behaviour that is 
illegal and for which municipal, 
provincial, or federal laws may 
apply. 
 
Examples may 
include, but are 
not limited to: 
- 
Physical 
assaults 
against 
another person 
(e.g., pushing, 
kicking, 
punching, 
hitting, etc.) 
- 
Threat to 
injure self or 
others (verbal 
or written) 
- 
Weapons 
possession 
including 
replicas 
- 
Use or selling 
of prescribed 
medicine(s) 
Depending on severity, the 
sanctions may be, but are not 
limited to: 
- 
Administrative Move/Relocation 
- 
Alcohol Probation 
- 
Apology 
- 
Ban from residence/campus 
- 
Behaviour Contract 
- 
Bond 
- 
Community Service hours 
- 
Educational Assignment 
- 
Expulsion from Residence or the 
College 
- 
Fines 
- 
Interim Measures 
- 
No communication or contact 
order 
- 
Non-academic suspension 
- 
Reduced privileges 
- 
Referral 
- 
Restitution 
- 
Written Warning 
Formal Resolution 
Procedure. 
All incidents must be 
