off-campus or at College related events. Residence students in violation of alcohol probation 
may face suspension or eviction from residence. Students who violate an alcohol probation will 
be placed on disciplinary probation automatically and future breaches of the Code may result in 
further sanctions being imposed. 
 
Apology – Apologies are meant to express the remorse of the person offering an apology and 
to help repair any damage that has been done to the parties’ relationship. Such apologies may 
be private (i.e., party-to-party), or public (i.e., to the Loyalist community), as appropriate. 
 
Bans – Students may be banned from one or more campus residences; from other areas on 
