Such measures can include, but are not restricted to, room/residence re-location; temporary 
room/residence/College ban; a No Contact/Communication Order; or other restrictions 
deemed necessary while the complaints process is underway. Interim measures, similar to 
emergency measures, do not imply a finding of guilt. 
 
No Communication Order – To safeguard the review and hearing process or to ensure a safe 
space for students involved in a complaint, the Vice-President, Student Life and Leadership, or 
Designate, may issue a No Communication Order. Such an order restricts, as outlined in the 
Order, communication between students involved in the complaint process until such time as 
