11. Relevant Legislation 
Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act (FIPPA) 
Ontario Human Rights Code 
Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA) 
 
APPENDIX A – DIRECT PARTY-TO-PARTY PROCEDURE 
Informal Party-to-Party Resolution 
Loyalist College recognizes that many disputes can be resolved informally without resorting to 
the procedures in this Code. Where it is possible and appropriate to do so, members of the 
College community are encouraged to use constructive communication to directly resolve the 
situation rather than invoking the formal complaints procedure under this Code. A suggested 
process for this is as follows: 
 
a. Choose a time and place when a conversation can proceed calmy, privately, and 
without too much time having passed from the time of the incident leading to 
the need for the meeting. Where appropriate, consider bringing another person 
