Student Life and Leadership, or Designate believes there are grounds for extending the 
deadline. Reasons for extending the time limit may include, but are not limited to, pending 
criminal proceedings; fear of/intimidation by the respondent(s); or an absence from the 
College by the Complainant. 
3. If it is determined by the Vice-President, Student Life and Leadership, or Designate, that the 
complaint falls within the scope of the Code, the Vice-President will notify the parties (refer 
to Appendix B). 
4. If the complaint does not fall within the scope of the Code but may fall within the scope of 
another College policy, the Complainant will be advised accordingly and provided with a 
