I. Postponement 
1. A hearing may be postponed, at the discretion of the Student Code of Conduct Complaints 
Review Panel, if it has independent reasons to do so or upon the request of one of the 
parties, provided the party satisfies the Panel that the postponement is necessary for a fair 
hearing to be held. When deciding whether to grant a postponement, the Complaints 
Review Panel shall consider the following factors: 
i. 
the timeliness of the request; 
ii. 
the adverse impact, if any, on other parties to the hearing; 
iii. 
whether postponements of the hearing have been previously granted; 
iv. 
the consent, lack thereof, of the parties; and  
