bias or perceived conflict-of-interest. If such a challenge is made, the entire Appeals Panel, 
absent the decision-maker whose impartiality is being questioned, will determine if the 
charge of reasonable apprehension of bias or conflict-of-interest is valid. Such decision shall 
be final. If no reasonable apprehension of bias or conflict-of-interest is found, the hearing 
shall proceed with all panel members as originally determined. If a reasonable 
apprehension of bias or conflict-of-interest is found, the hearing will be rescheduled, and a 
new Panel member provided. Or, if all parties agree, the hearing will proceed minus the 
