residence or campus under escort where appropriate permission(s) have been sought and 
granted. Other interim conditions may include, but are not limited to, restrictions on a 
student’s movement on-campus; no contact/communication orders; or suspension of 
student privileges; notification of external authorities (e.g., the police). 
5. The Vice-President, Student Life and Leadership, or Designate, may extend emergency 
measures until the Student Code of Conduct Complaints Review Panel or the Sole Decision-
Maker can reasonably hear the complaint. Normally, this will occur for a period not 
exceeding 30 business days from the date of the original imposition of emergency 
measures. 
