APPENDIX K – GUIDELINES FOR NATURAL JUSTICE 
1. The burden of proof in administrative hearings under this Code shall be on a balance of 
probabilities which is informally interpreted as what is most likely to have happened. If 
there is a belief that it is more likely than not that the incident occurred, the finding shall be 
the complaint is upheld. If there is a belief that it is less likely that the incident occurred, the 
finding shall be the complaint is denied. 
2. The process should proceed as quickly as possible providing each party’s right to due 
process is not negatively affected. 
3. Each party must be given sufficient notice as outlined in this Code. 
4. The student(s) must be informed of the case against them and be given the opportunity to 
prepare a response. 
