become involved with a student or group of students that is inconsistent with College policy. 
3.4.2 Academic employees are responsible for initiating efforts to resolve misunderstandings or conflicts
between themselves and any student. The academic employee will meet with the student, in a timely
manner, to discuss the problem and to explore options for resolution, maintaining an open, non-
confrontational attitude throughout the process. 
3.4.3 Should an academic employee and student be unable to resolve a misunderstanding or conflict, the
faculty will counsel the student to consider the next step in a resolution process.','{"source": "C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\Chatflix\\admin\\assets\\pdf\\d530fc75512458ee2c38572dd578b520.pdf",  "file_path": "C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\Chatflix\\admin\\assets\\pdf\\d530fc75512458ee2c38572dd578b520.pdf",  "page": 2,  "total_pages": 4,  "format": "PDF 1.4",  "title": "AOP 201 Code of Conduct: Academic Employees : Loyalist College",  "author": "",  "subject": "",  "keywords": "",  "creator": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML,  like Gecko) Chrome/126.0.0.0 Safari/537.36",  "producer": "Skia/PDF m126",  "creationDate": "D:20240722164431+00''00''",  "modDate": "D:20240722164431+00''00''",  "trapped": ""}','f128375e-c1de-4d37-8f7b-2711dd900976','3fc3e381-917e-4ce9-a397-acd0ed207df0');
