required however, the breadth of the role may vary depending on various factors, including, but not
limited to the credential, the number of programs/courses in a cluster, the number of faculty, number of
students, associated special projects, and external accreditation. Therefore, the exact nature of the
assignment will be negotiated individually with the Dean.   
5. Compensation to Academic Coordinators 
Academic Coordinators will be compensated as follows: 
Designated Coordinators will receive an allowance equal to one or two steps on the appropriate salary
schedule. The allowance will be in addition to their annual base salary. 
One-year certificate program – 1 step 
Two-year, three-year, or cluster programs – 2 steps 
