 Academic Freedom – the freedom of research; of legitimate classroom discussion and the advocacy of
alternative opinions in the College’s learning environment. 
 4. Policy Statement 
All College members including faculty, staff and students, shall support and protect this fundamental
principle and work collaboratively to provide an environment of tolerance and mutual respect. Every
member of the College should be able to work, teach and learn in an atmosphere which is free from
harassment and discrimination. 
Academic freedom includes protecting the rights of the teacher and of the student to learn. In research
and scholarship, academic freedom is critical to advancing knowledge. Academic freedom also includes
the right to freely communicate knowledge and the results of research and scholarship.
