Each academic Dean or designate is accountable for overseeing the Program Quality Assurance process
within their school.
The quality assurance process is a reflective, evidence-based process that supports the College’s ongoing
institutional focus on student learning, student success and program sustainability. Time and financial
support are required and participation in this process will be recognized. This is a sustainable process of
continual quality improvement across our academic programs and services.
This process creates evidence that is owned by the individual Schools and program teams. The evidence
respects the Schools’ or teams’ understanding of their program and disciplines. It includes a broad range
of stakeholder opinion – including, but not limited to, analysis of KPI data, focus groups, etc. – that leads
to clear recommendations on how the Schools and teams can improve their programs.
