person’s ability to conduct ethical research or make ethical decisions must be declared. 
Consent: before an individual becomes a participant in a research project, they must indicate their
permission or agreement. Ethical research requires free, informed and ongoing consent of participants. 
Ethics: principles of values used to define acceptable conduct. Ethical guidelines help distinguish
between good and bad, right or wrong. 
Minimal risk research: research in which there is an expectation the possible harm to participants will
be no greater than that encountered in daily life. 
Participant: an individual who has freely consented to be involved in a research study whereby data or
