Principles 
Notwithstanding the Tri-Agency Framework, all members of the College community involved in research
and scholarship are expected to adhere to ethical standards including, but not limited to, the following: 
4.1.1 Apply scholarly and scientific rigour and integrity when proposing, conducting, recording, analyzing,
transporting and storing data, and when publishing results. 
4.1.2 Recognize the substantive contributions of all collaborators; use unpublished work of other
researchers and scholars only with permission and due acknowledgement; and use archival material in
accordance with the rules of archival source. 
4.1.3 Ensure authorship of published work includes only individuals who have substantively contributed
