teaching, and testing involving animals. 
Research Ethics Board (REB) 
Reviews, and decides on, proposals for research using non-human subjects at the College, and
planned by College staff with collaborators elsewhere. 
Works closely with the ARI for establishing institutional policies on the care and use of non-human
subjects. 
The Board’s specific composition and function will accord with the requirements of its Terms of
Reference. 
College Animal Care Committee (CACC) 
Is the institutional body responsible for ensuring the humane care and use of animals in research,
teaching and testing, and has final authority to suspend any activity involving animals which does
