agreement. 
Exemption (Request Form is available online) ‘EX’ (Exemption) 
An EX is assigned in recognition of academic credit deemed by the College to be sufficiently similar
to program curriculum to warrant an exemption. Exemptions may also be available in certain
courses through a standard, established in-class assignment. 
Students must make application to the Pathways Coordinator for exemption(s) within the first 10
school days of the start of the academic semester. The student bears full responsibility for
acquiring and supplying all supporting documents (official transcripts, course descriptions, etc.) as
required for the purposes of evaluating a request for exemption. Courses approved for exemption
