application form (available on the student forms page of the College’s website) and submit it to
Enrolment Services who will advise of the re-admission decision in consultation with the relevant Dean.
There are two categories of re-admission to a program of study: re-admission for interrupted students in
good standing and re-admission for interrupted students required to withdraw.
5.4 Re-admission for Interrupted Students in Good Academic Standing
Students who let their registration in courses lapse, but have successfully completed previous
semesters and are in good standing, include the following:
students who fail to register in consecutive terms; and,
