11.5. Students who satisfactorily complete all academic requirements but, either by choice or by
circumstance, do not complete the required co-operative education work terms may graduate with a non-
co-operative education endorsed credential. Degree program students must complete their co-operative
education work term to be eligible for graduation.
11.6. Students enrolled in a mandatory co-op program, who are unable to participate in a co-op work term,
may be eligible to complete an applied project as an alternative.
Addendum: Acronyms and Terminology
