and/or any other members of the College or local community from risks or significant impact posed by
their behaviour. The College may need to take steps whether or not a violation under the Code of Student
Conduct has occurred. In some circumstances, placing a student on an involuntary leave of absence may
be an effective and appropriate course of action to address the situation until such time as the safety
concerns or other concerns are significantly mitigated. It is understood that this measure will be taken
only where other efforts have been unsuccessful and/or there is an urgent and immediate need to
ameliorate the risks. Additionally, this measure will be implemented only for as long as is necessary to
