Students shall be the owners of intellectual property rights in works they create, except in the following
situations: 
Where the College pays the students for the works they create, in which case the College shall own
the IP rights therein. 
Where the students use the College resources and facilities to create the works, outside of their
course requirements, in which case the students shall be required to obtain the College’s consent to
the use of its resources and facilities. It shall be a condition to the giving of such consent, that the
College and the students enter into an agreement for the creation of the works, which agreement
shall provide for, among other things, the ownership of any intellectual property rights in the works
to be created, the exploitation of the works by the students and the College, and the sharing of any
revenue by the students and the College from such exploitation. 
