12. Disclosure of Inventions 
Except for course materials created by employees, all other potentially valuable intellectual property
conceived or first reduced to practice by the College employees in the course of their duties, whether or
not the intellectual property in question is creator(s)-owned or College-owned, shall be disclosed to the
College. Initial disclosure may be done informally. At a later time, if the intellectual property is College-
owned, and the College expresses its interest in commercializing, a formal written disclosure will be
