5.4. No co-operative education program will require a student to begin the program with a work term.
5.5. A co-operative education program may end in a work term provided the work duties comply with the
principle of being integrated with the academic elements of the program and are evaluated accordingly
to ensure that the student has met the program learning outcomes/competencies.In exceptional
circumstances, co-operative education work terms may be combined to create a double or triple work
term provided the principle of integrating academic and work terms is maintained. This must be in
consultation with the Senior Vice-President, Academic (SVPA) and the Director, CS&WIL.
5.5.1. A student who leaves a terminal work term to take on employment with a different employer
