student’s supervisor for monitoring and evaluation purposes.
6.4. Employers are encouraged to inform the College promptly if the work performance of the student
does not meet agreed standards or if the student’s duties, or working conditions change substantially
from those described in the job description.
6.5. The employer will be required to participate in an evaluation of the co-op student’s performance of
the duties and objectives defined at the outset of the work term.
7. ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
7.1. Co-operative Education Students:
7.1.1. Submit a completed Release of Information Form to faculty representative prior to their first
work term.
