The Senior Vice President Academic will:
5.1 Ensure that effective performance requirements are in place in each School of the College to
ensure that PACs are created for every program of the College and that they are functioning in
accordance with the Ministry Binding Policy Directives.
5.2 Ensure that the President receives a summary report of each PAC’s activities in April of each
academic year.
5.3 Provide an annual report to the President, who will present the report to the Board of
Governors through the Academic Committee in May of each academic year.
5.4 Coordinate on behalf of the President, an annual meeting with PAC chairs and College
Leadership Team to discuss opportunities to build program quality and enhance student learning
and satisfaction.
6. Other Roles and Responsibilities
