if a college closure is necessary.
a. The safety of employees and students.
b. The ability of the College to maintain safe conditions.
c. Current and forecasted weather conditions.
d. Current and forecasted road conditions.
e. Public transportation availability.
4.2 Closing the College
If the college is closed, classes and examinations are suspended, college buildings are closed, meetings
and events are cancelled.   Students are to check communications from their professor/instructor for
details on how the missed class will be addressed.
Should this action be necessary, the College will provide as much notice as possible in the circumstance
to minimize inconvenience.
Note:  No change will be made to an employee’s status should they be on sick leave, vacation, leave,
