have not been specially trained to perform a specific job or task, they do not qualify as service animals
under AODA.
4.       Policy Statement
The College will make efforts to accommodate individuals to the point of undue hardship. In turn, there is
an expectation of good faith when requesting an accommodation for a support animal. A student or an
employee may seek accommodation for one service/support animal. Support animal requests must be
submitted annually. Examples of services provided by support/service animals include:
Mobility
Guidance to those with visual or hearing impairment
Emotional or psychological support (PTSD, autism, substance abuse)
Seizure response
