“Applied Research and Innovation Office” or “ARIO” means the research administration office of the
College.
“Applied Research” means research and development activities directed at solving a specific challenge
faced by an external partner or TPCE. Applied Research at colleges is typically carried out by teams of
students working under the guidance, supervision and mentorship of faculty, and in collaboration with
partner organizations or under agreement with TCPEs. Applied Research includes grant-funded and
industry sponsored Applied Research, curriculum-based research projects in collaboration with an
external organization and Applied Research carried out by faculty and staff on paid professional
development leave.
