“Third-Party Commercial Entities” or “TCPE” means businesses with which the College has contracted to
provide Applied Research Services that could result in Arising IP
.
4.       Policy Statement – General Principles
This policy is to be read in conjunction with the AOP 235 Intellectual Property, which addresses the
ownership of intellectual property developed by its employees and students.
4.1       Disclosure
All Creators have an obligation to promptly disclose Intellectual Property with commercial potential to the
College as per the procedure developed for disclosure to the ARIO or TCPE. For clarity, such disclosure is
not considered Public Disclosure.
Given that the responsibility to disclose rests with individuals, the College will educate potential Creators
on the importance of thorough and timely disclosure.
