Policy Title:
Including Indigenous
Knowledge and Community
Members in College Activities
Number:
ADMIN 126
Policy Sponsor: 
Office of the President
Supersedes Existing
Policy:
No
Associated Procedure:
Yes
Policy Owner:
Executive Director,
Indigenous
Initiatives and
Reconciliation
Next Review Date:
October 2026
Date Last Approved
by the CET:
October 4, 2023
1.       Purpose
Loyalist is committed to working collaboratively with Indigenous Elders, Knowledge Keepers, and
community members to build and support lasting relationships with Indigenous Peoples and
communities. After centuries of colonial practices that aimed to dispossess, assimilate, and oppress
Indigenous Peoples and their ways of life, it is essential that the College helps to create and support a
space for Indigenous knowledge in a welcoming, respectful, and culturally appropriate way.
